#: quickbook/templates/settings-admin.php:59
msgid ""
"This is a private address. That is fine if you are on the same network as "
"the server. If you opened this page from outside (for example a phone on "
"mobile data), Nextcloud does not know your reverse proxy: all visitors then "
"share one address, and the booking limit applies to all of them together. "
"Add the proxy to \"trusted_proxies\" in config.php."
msgstr ""

#: quickbook/templates/settings-admin.php:62
msgid ""
"This should be the public address of the device you are using right now. If "
"it is the address of your server or proxy instead, add the proxy to "
"\"trusted_proxies\" in config.php."
msgstr ""

#: quickbook/templates/settings-admin.php:65
msgid ""
"Share the Calendar's own booking links (\"Copy link\" in the Calendar app). "
"They open Quick Booking while it is on, and the Calendar booking page while "
"it is off, disabled or removed. Links to /apps/quickbook/book/… only work "
"while the app is installed."
msgstr ""
